      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "like वा in मृतः को N'i. S'a. 32. Cf. परैस्त्वदन्यः क इवापहारयेत् &c. Kir.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "I. 31. or कइव—what sort of. ( what reason have they for )",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "लेशेपि पतयः—the loc. is noteworthy; see Pàn. II. 3. 30. विषादे",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "कर्तव्ये-Mr. Telang here remarks—‘for having so little’ they",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "should have grieved; but it would be better to suppose that",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "they should have chiefly grieved for being the lords of भुक्तो-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "च्छिष्टा पृथ्वी.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 60. मृत्पिंडः &c.—The whole earth is a ball of clay",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "encircled by the line of water (sea); it is indeed, very small, and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "is parcelled out among themselves by a number of kings after",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "hundreds of fights. These petty chiefs are poor and mean-minded.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "The poet, therefore, despises those that wish to get something",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "out of them. स्वांशीकृत्य is preferable to भागीकृत्य-which simply",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "means ‘having divided.’",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 61. कोऽपि—indescribable, unnamable. स जातः आसीत्—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "he alone was born; he alone deserves to be counted as having",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "been born, the birth of others is as good as nothing. उच्चैः—on",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "high; or so as to give it high honour. अलंकारविधये—for the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "purpose of decoration, as a decoration or ornament. It is well-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "known that S'iva decorates himself with a string of the skulls",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "of those who fall on the battle-field &c; comp. कपालि वा स्यादथवे-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "न्दुशेखरम् । Kum. V. 78. That deity does not, however, give",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "preference to one skull in particular, nor does he wear it on his",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "head, as the poet seems to imply. प्रवण derived from प्रु 1 A. to go",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "+ल्युट् ( अन ) प्रवन्ते अनेन अत्र वा sloping ( प्रवणः क्रमनिम्नोर्व्यां प्रह्वे ना-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "तु चतुष्पथे । Amara; ), inclined, disposed; नृभिः नमद्भिः—instr.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "absolute, same as the loc. absolute, नृषु नमत्सु सत्सु or the inst.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 14,
          "text": "may be हेतौ ( the whole being equivalent to नृणां नमनैः as Mr.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 15,
          "text": "Telang has it. ) दर्पज्वरभरः—excess of feverish or morbid pride.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 62. प्रसादं नेतुम्-to propitiate. क्लेशकलिलम्—The confused",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "mass of misery. Cf. मोहकलिलम् Bhg. XI. 52, कलते कल्यते वा;",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "कल्+इल ( च् ); Un I 54. कलिलं गहनं समे । Amara. Mr. Telang",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "reads कलितम्. He says ‘कलितं might mean बन्धन but this re-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "quires a straining’. स्वयमुदित &c.—चिन्तामणि is a jewel the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "possession of which is believed to give any desired object.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
